module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.LargeColimits

/-!
# A colimit of abelian groups is generated by the images of its injections

Every element of a colimit of abelian groups is a finite sum of elements of the images of the
colimit injections, for an arbitrary index category — no filteredness and no directedness of the
index is needed. This is what replaces the filtered-colimit description of an element of a colimit
when the index is only a partially ordered set: a filtered colimit has every element in the image
of a *single* injection, whereas in general one gets a finite sum.

## Main definitions

* `AddCommGrpCat.colimitListSum` — the element of a colimit named by a list of pairs (an index, an
  element of the corresponding term of the diagram).

## Main results

* `AddCommGrpCat.exists_colimitListSum_eq` — every element of the colimit is the value of such a
  list.

## Implementation notes

The proof is Mathlib's presentation of a colimit of abelian groups as a quotient of the direct sum:
`AddCommGrpCat.isColimit_iff_bijective_desc` says that a cocone is colimiting exactly when the
induced map out of `AddCommGrpCat.Colimits.Quot` is bijective, and its forward direction applied to
`CategoryTheory.Limits.colimit.isColimit` makes that map surjective on the strength of
`CategoryTheory.Limits.HasColimit` alone. A representative in `Quot` is a `DFinsupp`, and
`DFinsupp.sum_single` writes it as a finite sum of the images of the generators.

So the hypotheses are exactly `HasColimit`: no `DecidableEq` on the index (`classical` inside the
proof suffices, the statement not mentioning `Quot`), and no smallness of the index beyond whatever
the colimit's existence already required.

A finite family of generators is recorded as a `List ((j : J) × ↑(D.obj j))` because the consumer
pushes it through a further homomorphism with `map_list_sum` and `List.map_map`. The proof actually
produces a family with *distinct* indices — the support of the `DFinsupp` representative — and that
sharper form is available directly from `AddCommGrpCat.isColimit_iff_bijective_desc` should a
consumer need it; it is not stated here because none does.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F6M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F6M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F6P](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F6P)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe w v u

namespace AddCommGrpCat

open Colimits

variable {J : Type u} [Category.{v} J] (D : J ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w}) [HasColimit D]

/-- The element of a colimit of abelian groups named by a list of pairs, each pair being an index
together with an element of the corresponding term of the diagram: the sum of the images of the
second components under the corresponding colimit injections. -/
public def colimitListSum (l : List ((j : J) × ↑(D.obj j))) : ↑(colimit D) :=
  (l.map (fun p => (colimit.ι D p.1) p.2)).sum

/-- The value of a list of generators, unfolded. -/
public theorem colimitListSum_eq (l : List ((j : J) × ↑(D.obj j))) :
    colimitListSum D l = (l.map (fun p => (colimit.ι D p.1) p.2)).sum := rfl

/-- Every element of a colimit of abelian groups is a finite sum of images of elements of the terms
of the diagram, with no assumption on the index category beyond the existence of the colimit. -/
public theorem exists_colimitListSum_eq (g : ↑(colimit D)) :
    ∃ l : List ((j : J) × ↑(D.obj j)), colimitListSum D l = g := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := ((AddCommGrpCat.isColimit_iff_bijective_desc (F := D)
    (colimit.cocone D)).mp ⟨colimit.isColimit D⟩).2 g
  induction q using QuotientAddGroup.induction_on with
  | H x =>
    refine ⟨x.support.toList.map (fun j => (⟨j, x j⟩ : (j : J) × ↑(D.obj j))), ?_⟩
    rw [colimitListSum_eq, ← hq, List.map_map]
    have hx : (QuotientAddGroup.mk x : Colimits.Quot D) =
        ∑ j ∈ x.support, Colimits.Quot.ι D j (x j) := by
      conv_lhs => rw [← DFinsupp.sum_single (f := x)]
      rw [DFinsupp.sum, ← QuotientAddGroup.mk'_apply, map_sum]
      rfl
    rw [hx, map_sum, ← Finset.sum_map_toList]
    exact congrArg List.sum
      (List.map_congr_left fun j _ => (Colimits.Quot.ι_desc D (colimit.cocone D) j (x j)).symm)

end AddCommGrpCat

end
